{"kind":"report","text":"Checker review of the invitation engine's wait at head 8c2fde64, for request e9f268d9 and review request 709d56fd. Verdict: APPROVED. The wait is bounded, signs no act, stops the same way at its end, and replaces the script's recheck. This is hosted code. It may land, and no deployment of it may happen during the hosted agent's run.\n\n## Your five questions\n\n1. **Widening to `not-found` and `forbidden`: acceptable, and I would have asked for it.** Stopping there would keep the failure this head removes. A lasting `forbidden`, such as a key that lost its standing, can be a real refusal, and it costs 20 seconds before the same `unknown` that it reached before. That is a delay and no wrong answer. Neither answer needs to stop at once. Every other read answer still stops at once.\n2. **The claim: exact.** `activeInbox` calls only `inboxOfOpening`, which only reads. The note's sentence states the session request and the signed reads. One detail for a reader: `reads.ts` forgets a session on `forbidden`, so a scope with no index can make one session request per read through the wait. The deployed path answers `not-found` first, so I expect that case to be rare, and the note's \"fails a read check\" covers it.\n3. **Removing the recheck and `inboxRechecks`: no recovery rests on them.** No use of either name remains under `examples`, `packages`, `apps`, `docs` or `scripts`. The runbook's recovery is `check` and `continue`, as before. The enrollment note keeps its old statements, and you are right to leave a note that records its own head.\n4. **Words during the wait: no.** The page already says \"Working on the connection\", with the buttons disabled, for the whole call. That sentence stays true for 20 seconds.\n5. **The second room's 404: enough, as the note states it.** The note says that the answer fits the index by reading the code, and that no run has shown the cause. Do not say more than that.\n\n## Other points I checked\n\n- **`Context.tries`.** Production callers do not lower this wait: `start-custody.ts` and `connection-custody.ts` only pass a caller's value through, and `claim.ts`'s `tries: 1` is its own read-only path. I did not trace every test option.\n- **The page's fence.** Each read goes through `wait(options, ...)`, so a room change stops the wait at the next read, at most about one second later.\n- **`enrolKey`.** It refuses a pending inbox with the same `bad()`, and issuance writes a link only after it read an active inbox.\n- **The reordered read.** `inboxOfOpening` now reads entry 0 only after `active`. The updated comment in `diagnostics.ts` states the new meaning of the last read.\n- **The hosted witness.** Head bed1c8be keeps its own `invite-agent` recheck and is unaffected. After this head lands, that recheck adds nothing, but my approval 9821f0e4 covers the head as it stands, so leave it for this run.\n\n## Conclusions\n\n**Architecture.** Sound. The wait belongs in the engine, where the page and the script both meet it, and the script loses code.\n\n**Security.** No issue. The wait adds no act, no credential and no new read authority. The seal of `invitations.ts` in `security-entry-points.test.mjs` moves with it, and that test passes.\n\n**Simplification.** Good. The head removes one loop, one receipt field and two constants.\n\n## What I checked\n\n- **Read.** The diff of `invitations.ts`, `identities.ts`, `diagnostics.ts`, the runbook and the seal, the note, the page's status words and the `tries` callers. I did not read the new test bodies.\n- **Evidence.** `SHA256SUMS` hashes to `c5eb2519…`, each listed file verifies, and no file is writable. The gate's head is `6c4a3f14`, it exited 0, and its log shows 3262 plain and 929 native tests. The diff from there to this head touches only the note and its manifest. `controls/results.json` holds 20 rows, all red by an assertion. I read those results and did not rerun them.\n- **Tests I ran at this head.** `identities.test.ts` passes 21 of 21. `agent-key.scope.test.ts` and `start.scope.test.ts` pass 7 of 7. `security-entry-points.test.mjs` passes 10 with 0 failures. `check-notes` reports 0 warnings, `check-doc-links` 0 broken links, and `check-commit-messages` 0 flagged. The worktree stayed clean. The head includes main de53d89a.\n- **Not done.** I used no independent reader, and I ran no control. No Worker, real room or browser has run this wait.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:7b9cf538fa0eabfa98b8a993bebbb22ca98b2a41","binding":"assigned","head":"8c2fde64a4584d1d1fd8eea7991ba261898526b6","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:8938ad77819c9b91941331fb2575c932ddb59942\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:93b27693777abb69a2f4d524a53f2f1dc9b4e918\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:8938ad77819c9b91941331fb2575c932ddb59942","review_path":"reviewguard@1","stale":"true","stale_bases":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:08a66cb04ab50d8968de73247113c275cb8d0580, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:0f1a98950662d72327e0237eee98c807b7f65b3c, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:1a6531fed7a047a3d40dcad1b2d26bb90495760c, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:41c6c25c9012bcba97075aaec367f767ce3b5c89, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:44f49fed1aa58956a4c7dd445c766c5d26a4328c, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:709d56fdb18eb5f5c19a4fac04f3d811a2c3877b, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:7b9cf538fa0eabfa98b8a993bebbb22ca98b2a41, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:8938ad77819c9b91941331fb2575c932ddb59942, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:93c5d92aba9f6f9dea7a181efd1cc583987f469f, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f757237